Feature: Ship a reservation
  The order system ships a reservation in full, or the stated quantity per line. The shell loads the
  reservation and the stored level of each of its lines.

  Scenario: A reservation ships in full
    When I run "ship_reservation" with:
      | caller.role  | now                      | idempotency_key | reservation_id                       | stored_reservation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | stored_levels                                                                                                                                                                                     |
      | order_system | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | ship-0001       | 3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13 | {"reservation_id": "3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13", "order_id": "ORD-1", "state": "ACTIVE", "reservation_lines": [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10, "shipped": 0}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "quantity": 5, "shipped": 0}], "expires_at": "2026-11-22T10:30:00.000Z"} | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 100, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] |
    Then the output is "reservation_changed":
      | levels                                                                                                                                                                                           |
      | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 490, "reserved": 90, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 45, "reserved": 35, "available": 10}] |

  Scenario: A stated quantity of a line ships part of the reservation
    When I run "ship_reservation" with:
      | caller.role  | now                      | idempotency_key | reservation_id                       | stored_reservation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | stored_levels                                                                                                                                                                                     | ship_lines                                                     |
      | order_system | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | ship-0001       | 3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13 | {"reservation_id": "3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13", "order_id": "ORD-1", "state": "ACTIVE", "reservation_lines": [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10, "shipped": 0}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "quantity": 5, "shipped": 0}], "expires_at": "2026-11-22T10:30:00.000Z"} | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 100, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 4}] |
    Then the output is "reservation_changed":
      | levels                                                                                            |
      | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 496, "reserved": 96, "available": 400}] |

  Scenario: The last units of a partly shipped reservation ship it
    When I run "ship_reservation" with:
      | caller.role  | now                      | idempotency_key | reservation_id                       | stored_reservation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | stored_levels                                                                                                                                                                                     | ship_lines                                                     |
      | order_system | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | ship-0001       | 3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13 | {"reservation_id": "3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13", "order_id": "ORD-1", "state": "PARTIALLY_SHIPPED", "reservation_lines": [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10, "shipped": 4}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "quantity": 5, "shipped": 5}], "expires_at": "2026-11-22T10:30:00.000Z"} | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 100, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 6}] |
    Then the output is "reservation_changed":
      | levels                                                                                            |
      | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 494, "reserved": 94, "available": 400}] |

  Scenario Outline: A line that asks for more than the reservation holds is refused
    When I run "ship_reservation" with:
      | caller.role  | now                      | idempotency_key | reservation_id                       | stored_reservation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | stored_levels                                                                                                                                                                                     | ship_lines   |
      | order_system | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | ship-0001       | 3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13 | {"reservation_id": "3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13", "order_id": "ORD-1", "state": "PARTIALLY_SHIPPED", "reservation_lines": [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10, "shipped": 4}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "quantity": 5, "shipped": 5}], "expires_at": "2026-11-22T10:30:00.000Z"} | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 100, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] | <ship_lines> |
    Then the output is "invalid_request":
      | error_code      |
      | INVALID_REQUEST |

    Examples:
      | ship_lines                                                      |
      | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 7}]  |
      | [{"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "quantity": 1}]  |
      | [{"sku": "OTHER-SKU", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 1}] |

  Scenario: An unknown reservation is not found
    When I run "ship_reservation" with:
      | caller.role  | now                      | idempotency_key | reservation_id                       | stored_levels                                                                                                                                                                                     |
      | order_system | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | ship-0001       | 3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13 | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 100, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] |
    Then the output is "reservation_not_found":
      | error_code            | reservation_id                       |
      | RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND | 3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13 |

  Scenario Outline: A shipped, released or expired reservation cannot be shipped
    When I run "ship_reservation" with:
      | caller.role  | now                      | idempotency_key | reservation_id                       | stored_reservation   | stored_levels                                                                                                                                                                                     |
      | order_system | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | ship-0001       | 3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13 | <stored_reservation> | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 100, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] |
    Then the output is "invalid_state":
      | error_code    | state   |
      | INVALID_STATE | <state> |

    Examples:
      | state    | stored_reservation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
      | SHIPPED  | {"reservation_id": "3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13", "order_id": "ORD-1", "state": "SHIPPED", "reservation_lines": [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10, "shipped": 10}], "expires_at": "2026-11-22T10:30:00.000Z"} |
      | RELEASED | {"reservation_id": "3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13", "order_id": "ORD-1", "state": "RELEASED", "reservation_lines": [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10, "shipped": 0}], "expires_at": "2026-11-22T10:30:00.000Z"} |
      | EXPIRED  | {"reservation_id": "3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13", "order_id": "ORD-1", "state": "EXPIRED", "reservation_lines": [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10, "shipped": 0}], "expires_at": "2026-11-22T10:30:00.000Z"}  |

  Scenario Outline: Another caller may not ship a reservation
    When I run "ship_reservation" with:
      | caller.role | now                      | idempotency_key | reservation_id                       | stored_reservation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | stored_levels                                                                                                                                                                                     |
      | <role>      | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | ship-0001       | 3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13 | {"reservation_id": "3f2b8c1e-9a4d-4c7e-8b1f-2d6e5a9c0b13", "order_id": "ORD-1", "state": "ACTIVE", "reservation_lines": [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10, "shipped": 0}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "quantity": 5, "shipped": 0}], "expires_at": "2026-11-22T10:30:00.000Z"} | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 100, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] |
    Then the output is "forbidden":
      | error_code | role   |
      | FORBIDDEN  | <role> |

    Examples:
      | role            |
      | warehouse_staff |
      | clock           |

